  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1243 AM CDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nDense fog over the southern half of the area this morning was\nconstrained to the humid airmass ahead of the cold front. That\nfog has since dissipated with the morning insolation and \nmixing. \n\nSfc high settles into the area today, with subsidence keeping\nskies mostly clear. The widespread sunny skies won't be enough \nto make up for the slightly cooler air in place today behind \nthat cold front. High temperatures will range from near 80 to \nmid-80s along Kansas and South Dakota. Northerly winds of 5-10 \nmph will become light and variable overnight. Model guidance has\nsome fog development in southern Iowa and northwest Missouri \novernight where dewpoints will remain higher. Have added patchy\nfog in overnight to western Iowa.",
